Zoe's event-causal modules are independent Python adaptations, not the original iLab implementation and not a claim of endorsement by USC or iLab. VisualCortex, Brain, saliency, Bayesian surprise, visual memory, component composition, Beowulf, and reference tests inform the architecture; new event reconstruction, temporal prediction, independent uncertainty, gated plasticity, and evidence guards are Zoe-specific work. `ILAB-INTEGRATION.md` and `evidence/ilab/catalog.json` preserve per-file classification and reference-build modifications.

